#### Review Checklist
- [ ] TypeScript types are properly defined
- [ ] Components follow naming conventions
- [ ] Error handling is implemented
- [ ] Loading states are handled
- [ ] Accessibility requirements are met
- [ ] Performance considerations are addressed
- [ ] Tests are included (if applicable)
- [ ] Documentation is updated

### 15. Documentation

#### Code Documentation
- Use JSDoc for complex functions
- Document component props
- Explain business logic
- Keep README updated

#### API Documentation
- Document all endpoints
- Include request/response examples
- Explain error codes
- Provide usage examples

## Common Patterns

### Video Player Component
```typescript
interface VideoPlayerProps {
  video: VideoType;
  onProgress?: (progress: number) => void;
  onEnd?: () => void;
  autoplay?: boolean;
}

export default function VideoPlayer({ video, onProgress, onEnd, autoplay }: VideoPlayerProps) {
  // Implementation
}
```

### API Request Hook
```typescript
export function useApiRequest<T>(endpoint: string, options?: RequestOptions) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: [endpoint],
    queryFn: () => apiRequest<T>(endpoint),
    ...options
  });
}
```

### Form Validation
```typescript
import { z } from "zod";
import { useForm } from "react-hook-form";
import { zodResolver } from "@hookform/resolvers/zod";

const formSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1, "Title is required"),
  description: z.string().optional(),
  category: z.enum(["Ramayana", "Krishna", "Mahabharata"]),
});

type FormData = z.infer<typeof formSchema>;
```

## Troubleshooting

### Common Issues
1. **TypeScript errors**: Check import paths and type definitions
2. **Build failures**: Verify all dependencies are installed
3. **API errors**: Check server logs and network requests
4. **Styling issues**: Verify Tailwind classes and CSS imports

### Debug Tools
- React Developer Tools
- Network tab for API debugging
- Console for error messages
- Drizzle Studio for database inspection

